---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const differences = [
  {
    label: "The purpose of assessment",
    traditional: "Measure performance at a few points in time",
    onTrack: "Create, guide, and validate learning throughout a student's journey",
  },
  {
    label: "How achievement is judged",
    traditional: "Accumulate enough marks across separate assessments",
    onTrack: "Demonstrate the required capabilities through a connected body of evidence",
  },
  {
    label: "What happens after feedback",
    traditional: "The mark is usually final, and feedback explains what the student could have done",
    onTrack: "Students act on feedback, revise their work, and strengthen their understanding",
  },
  {
    label: "The role of teaching staff",
    traditional: "Judge completed work after submission",
    onTrack: "Coach learning as it develops, and validate achievement along the way",
  },
  {
    label: "What the final grade means",
    traditional: "Strong performance in one area can compensate for gaps in another",
    onTrack: "All required capabilities must be demonstrated; important learning is not averaged away",
  },
];

const gradeBands = [
  {
    grade: "Pass",
    requirement: "Complete all Pass tasks",
  },
  {
    grade: "Credit",
    requirement: "Pass tasks + Credit tasks",
  },
  {
    grade: "Distinction",
    requirement: "Pass + Credit + Distinction tasks",
  },
  {
    grade: "High Distinction",
    requirement: "Complete every task",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout>
  <main class="not-prose bg-white text-slate-700">
    <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-white text-slate-700">
      <div
        class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 -z-10 h-96 bg-gradient-to-b from-blue-50 to-white"
        aria-hidden="true"
      ></div>

      <div class="mx-auto max-w-screen-2xl px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl text-center">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-700">The OnTrack difference</p>
          <h1 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-blue-950 text-balance sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
            From accumulating marks to building capability
          </h1>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600 sm:text-xl">
            Traditional assessment samples student performance at a few high-stakes moments. The OnTrack Education Framework makes learning visible throughout the unit, so students can improve and educators can build confidence in what they have achieved.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-7xl gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="h-full rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 border-t-4 border-t-slate-400 bg-white p-7 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Traditional assessment</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-blue-950 lg:whitespace-nowrap 2xl:text-3xl">Submit. Receive a mark. Move on.</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600">
              Learning is interrupted by a small number of weighted assessments. Each mark contributes to an overall total.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="h-full rounded-3xl border border-blue-200 border-t-4 border-t-blue-600 bg-blue-50 p-7 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700">OnTrack</p>
            <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-blue-950 lg:whitespace-nowrap 2xl:text-3xl">Attempt. Receive guidance. Improve.</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">
              Assessment becomes part of learning. Students build a portfolio of trusted evidence through active tasks, feedback, discussion, and revision.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-slate-100 bg-white py-16 text-slate-700 sm:py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 sm:px-8 lg:px-12">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-blue-950 text-balance sm:text-4xl">
            Create learning, don't just measure it
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
            OnTrack changes the relationship between learning, feedback, and judgement. The standard remains clear; what changes is how students are supported to reach it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-6xl overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
          <div class="hidden grid-cols-[1.15fr_1fr_1fr] bg-slate-50 text-sm font-semibold md:grid">
            <div class="p-5 text-slate-500">What changes</div>
            <div class="border-l border-slate-200 p-5 text-slate-700">Traditional assessment</div>
            <div class="border-l border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 p-5 text-blue-950">OnTrack Education Framework</div>
          </div>

          {differences.map((item) => (
            <article class="grid border-t border-slate-200 first:border-t-0 md:grid-cols-[1.15fr_1fr_1fr]">
              <h3 class="p-5 font-semibold text-blue-950 md:p-6">{item.label}</h3>
              <div class="border-t border-slate-100 p-5 md:border-l md:border-t-0 md:p-6">
                <p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-600 md:hidden">Traditional</p>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-600">{item.traditional}</p>
              </div>
              <div class="border-t border-blue-100 bg-blue-50/60 p-5 md:border-l md:border-t-0 md:p-6">
                <p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 md:hidden">OnTrack</p>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-700">{item.onTrack}</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-y border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 py-16 text-slate-700 sm:py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 sm:px-8 lg:px-12">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-700">Designed for learning</p>
          <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-blue-950 text-balance sm:text-4xl">
            Flexible in format. Consistent in purpose.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
            OnTrack can adapt to different teaching contexts while keeping active learning, meaningful feedback, and trusted evidence at its core.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-6xl gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
          <div class="border-t-2 border-blue-200 pt-6">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-700">Flexible by design</p>
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-blue-950 text-balance sm:text-3xl">
              A framework, not a fixed teaching format
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
              OnTrack defines how learning is developed, evidenced, supported, and validated. It does not prescribe a single way to deliver content.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600">
              A unit can be weekly or self-paced, face-to-face, online, flipped or more traditionally structured. What connects every OnTrack design is a coherent sequence of active tasks, regular staff–student touchpoints, opportunities to improve, and a portfolio of trusted evidence.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t-2 border-blue-200 pt-6">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-700">Progress through feedback</p>
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-blue-950 text-balance sm:text-3xl">
              “Not yet” is a next step, not a dead end
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
              Each task is judged against clear criteria. When the evidence is sufficient, the task is complete. When it is not yet sufficient, the student receives guidance and another opportunity to demonstrate the standard.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-blue-950" aria-label="Attempt, feedback, improve, complete">
              <span>Attempt</span>
              <span class="text-blue-300" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <span>Feedback</span>
              <span class="text-blue-300" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <span>Improve</span>
              <span class="text-blue-300" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <span>Complete</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-16 text-slate-700 sm:py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 sm:px-8 lg:px-12">
        <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:gap-16">
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-700">Grades represent achievement</p>
            <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-blue-950 text-balance sm:text-4xl">
              Students know what each grade requires
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
              Tasks are aligned to learning outcomes and, where ranked grades are used, to grade-level standards. Rather than simply collecting enough marks to cross a numerical threshold, students complete all the tasks  required at that level to achieve that grade.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-600">
              This prevents strong performance in one area from concealing an important gap elsewhere. Once every required task for a grade level is complete, the student has secured at least that grade.
            </p>
          </div>

          <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-3 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-slate-100 sm:p-5">
            <video
              class="h-auto w-full rounded-2xl bg-white"
              autoplay
              muted
              loop
              playsinline
              preload="metadata"
              aria-label="Animation showing a task moving through submission, feedback, revision, and completion"
            >
              <source src="/ContentImages/TaskAssessmentGif.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 overflow-hidden border-y border-slate-200 md:grid md:grid-cols-4 md:divide-x md:divide-slate-200">
          {gradeBands.map((band, index) => (
            <article class="flex gap-4 border-t border-slate-200 py-6 first:border-t-0 md:block md:border-t-0 md:px-6 md:py-8 md:first:pl-0 md:last:pr-0">
              <span class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-sm font-semibold text-blue-800">
                {index + 1}
              </span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-blue-950 md:mt-4">{band.grade}</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">{band.requirement}</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
          The exact grade structure can be adapted to the needs of each learning context.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 py-16 text-slate-700 sm:py-20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 sm:px-8 lg:px-12">
        <div class="text-center">
          <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-blue-950 text-balance sm:text-4xl">
            How we introduce OnTrack to students
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-950 shadow-lg ring-1 ring-slate-200">
          <div class="aspect-video">
            <iframe
              class="h-full w-full"
              src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/GMDU4_D-uKY"
              title="Introduction to learning with the OnTrack Education Framework"
              loading="lazy"
              allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
              referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
              allowfullscreen
            ></iframe>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>